<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani sugar mill stocks fall sharply.</title>
<headline>Pakistani sugar mill stocks fall sharply.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Sunday the stocks of refined crystal white sugar from the 1995/96 (July-June) production of 2.47 million tonnes fell to 0.66 million tonnes by September 30.</p>
<p>Dealers had lifted 2.403 million tonnes, or 97.31 percent, of the production, and the remaining 66,375 tonnes, or 2.69 percent, remained within the mills, the association said.</p>
<p>Sugar mills plan to start the 1996/97 sugarcane crushing early next month.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
